=== PARITY (vs web SpeedProfileWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (SpeedProfileSource -> SpeedProfileModel):
    useSpeedProfile, useVehicles, useUnits, useTranslation, useDriving. The production app wires
    SpeedProfileSource over the KMP analytics store (/analytics/speed-profile) + the units preference
    (StateHolderModel<LoadableState<...>>); the view performs NO HTTP. No direct transport in the view.
  Projection -> SpeedProfileBuilder is a 1:1 port of the web derive block, EXECUTED-green (39/39, step [1]):
    convertSpeedFromSI: km/h = mps*3600/1000, mph = mps*3600/1609.344;
    formatBucketLabel: "lo-hi" -> "conv(lo)-conv(hi)", "N+" -> "conv(N)+", else verbatim (fmtInt = grouped 0dp);
    bars: frequency% = readings/sum(readings)*100, efficiency = avg_power_kw;
    peakFrequency = max(frequency), peakBucket = first bar at that frequency;
    sweetSpot = optimalSpeedMps>0 ? fmtInt(conv(optimal)) : lowest-positive-efficiency bucket, else "—";
    hasData = bars nonempty && any frequency>0.  parseLeadingDouble reproduces JS parseFloat ("80+" -> 80).
  Composition -> WidgetShell chrome (Activity icon -> SF "waveform.path.ecg" + "Speed Profile" title + freshness
    chip + refresh + optional "Open") · standard (>=2 cols) stat row [Most Common / Peak Freq / Sweet Spot] +
    composed chart + series legend · compact (cols<=1, kept for source fidelity) summary [Most Common / Sweet Spot].
  Chart -> web Recharts ComposedChart -> Swift Charts: frequency BarMark on the leading percent axis + the
    avg-power LineMark+PointMark overlaid on a NORMALIZED trailing axis (Swift Charts shares one y-domain, so the
    efficiency series is scaled into the frequency band for drawing and the trailing axis is labelled back in
    efficiency units — web right-axis tickFormatter). Categorical x = bucket labels (explicit domain preserves
    order), thinned on narrow widgets (web axisTick<->axisTickSm). Recharts hover tooltip -> persistent touch/
    VoiceOver-friendly legend (Frequency / Wh/mi). Colors map web indigo/amber -> design tokens
    Color.TS.chartSeriesSpeed / chartSeriesEnergy (P1/S9) — no inline hex (prohibited-pattern #1/#11 clean).
  Shared components -> reuses the REAL apps/apple library: Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSSkeleton +
